WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.025
The DISA STIG for NIOS 9 is
narrower than people assume.

2
00:00:04.025 --> 00:00:08.706
Release one, accepted in August
2026, has forty-five rules,

3
00:00:08.706 --> 00:00:12.988
and it covers only the
appliance's DNS capabilities.

4
00:00:12.988 --> 00:00:16.520
DHCP and address management
hardening aren't in it,

5
00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:19.463
so those rely on the
program's own baseline.

6
00:00:19.463 --> 00:00:24.997
The five most serious rules cover keeping
the Grid Master hidden unless keys are on

7
00:00:24.997 --> 00:00:29.890
an HSM, DNSSEC validation, running the
approved long-term-support version,

8
00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:32.537
validated cryptography, and no DSA keys.

9
00:00:32.537 --> 00:00:37.300
The rest cover zone transfers,
dynamic updates, keeping internal and

10
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:42.063
external roles apart, administrator
sign-in, logging and resilience.

11
00:00:42.063 --> 00:00:45.518
One practical tip: check these
settings at the zone level,

12
00:00:45.518 --> 00:00:47.062
not only at the Grid level.

13
00:00:47.062 --> 00:00:49.060
Next, FIPS mode.
